# TBH HUD — improvement.log
Updated 2026-06-11 (cowork, session 13 · app v1.0.4). Read-only companion for "TBH: Task Bar Hero" (v1.00.11).
Repo: revenantcabal-rgb/taskbarheroburat. Full detail: CLAUDE.md (facts + per-session DONE), docs/PRD.md, docs/PROGRESS.md.

## WHERE WE ARE (verified vs repo + live save — not claimed)
Read-only, calibrated. WEB ships on every push (GitHub Pages + the owner's Vercel project auto-deploys); **DESKTOP v1.0.4**
released (installer + latest.yml + blockmap → existing installs auto-update). **11 tabs** (Overview / Party / Inventory /
Loot / Runes / **Advisor** / Lifetime / Trends / **Crew** / Codex / Tips) render vs the test live save with 0 console errors.
**Crew API live** (Vercel serverless + Neon Postgres, opt-in only).

## CHANGELOG
Golden rule throughout: every number calibrated from the game's own data, or omitted — never fabricated.
- **S16 (v1.0.9) — offline vs online, researched + productized.** RESEARCH on both real histories: saves only
  exist while the game runs, so offline progress arrives as ONE lump at reopen; continuous-play pairs show
  wall-vs-played jitter of 0.0–0.15h while pairs containing a real restart show 0.49h+ AND their "other"-bucket
  gold delta matched Player.log offline collections EXACTLY (+235 == gold=235) → (a) offline gold provably lands
  in Sub2/3 and never touches the combat counter (per-stage GOLD/hr was already offline-proof), (b) wall−played
  > 0.25h is a calibrated closed-game detector. ADJUSTMENTS: per-stage rates now EXCLUDE offline-spanning
  intervals from XP and kill attribution (the reopen lump-sum — possibly containing offline XP, unverifiable —
  can't masquerade as farming; gold attribution kept, it's the proven-immune counter; kills/hr now uses its own
  hour base). NEW Trends section **"Online vs offline"**: played vs away hours + farming gold vs offline-reward
  gold (measured over the history window) + recent away gaps with the gold each brought + the exact per-collection
  table from Player.log. Crew: rows older than 24h are dimmed + a note that a member's row freezes while their
  HUD is offline and catches up (offline gains included) when they return. Honesty fix: the "offline rewards"
  game tip claimed gold AND XP — only gold is verified (Player.log records only gold) → reworded. Demo gained a
  realistic night-away gap; verify_save asserts the new summary's invariants (still PASS on both saves).
- **S15 (v1.0.8) — owner's next 4.** (1) **Crew shows play hours** (chip on every member + a "Play hours" rank
  option; the payload already carried it). (2) **Per-tier gear breakdown** — crew chips + Flex card now show
  "2 Immortal · 6 Legendary"-style counts; `trophies`/`tierCounts` are explicitly GEAR-ONLY in both engines so
  rarity-NAMED materials ("Scroll of Immortal Inscription", "Immortal Material") can never count toward flexing
  (verify_save asserts it + that tier counts sum to the trophy count); server whitelists the new `tiers` field.
  (3) **Loot origin inference** — the save has no origin flag (the old honest deferral stands), but the Cube
  CONSUMES material instances: the tracker now remembers each instance's material-ness, and one new gear piece +
  ≥9 material instances vanishing in the same save update = the Cube synthesis pattern → "⚒️ Cube (likely)";
  new items with nothing consumed → "✦ found" (drop or market — still indistinguishable); mixed reads stay
  untagged. New Origin column on the Loot table; the rare-alert notification no longer says "drop".
  (4) Best-gold/XP farming suggestions — already shipped in v1.0.7 (Tips/Overview/Trends/Lifetime).
- **S14 (v1.0.7) — owner's 4 asks.** (1) **Advisor equip-gating:** an item's Level reads as its equip requirement
  (calibrated: 43/43 equipped instances across both real saves satisfy lvl<=heroLevel, zero counterexamples) —
  upgrades the hero can't wear yet moved to a "Better gear waiting (level-locked)" notice (🔒 needs Lv X · now Lv Y),
  never advised; the tab badge counts equip-ready only. The old bad call (War Axe L20 advised to a L15 Slayer) is now
  the showcase locked notice. (2) Removed the obsolete "Stages read as Act X-Y" game tip. (3) **Best gold/hr + best
  XP/hr surfaced as suggestions:** trendPoint gained `xp` (every hero's cumulative XP summed via the calibrated level
  curve; delta = XP actually gained) → per-stage **XP/hr** alongside gold/hr + kills/hr (Trends bars, Lifetime,
  Overview one-liner), a **session XP/hr card**, and Tips suggestions ("switch to X for better gold/hr" only when the
  best measured stage differs from the current one; best-XP/hr informational). (4) **Enchanting workshop revamp:**
  compact per-hero open-slot rows (item minis with open-count badges) + **"Your enchanting stones"** — the gem
  materials you own with the game's own per-category effects (Weapon/Armor/Accessory/Any gear) and "✓ ready to use"
  matches where the slot category is calibrated (weapon types from the game's hero table; helmet/armor observed in
  the save's own EnchantData — every applied enchant's MaterialKey resolved to a stone and the rolled stat equaled
  that stone's category effect, 4/4 across both saves). Honest empty state + Codex pointer when no stones owned.
  Verified: verify_save PASS (new level-rule + xp invariants); browser == Node on the real save; ?demo shows
  ready+locked+stones; 11 tabs, 0 console errors, 0 overflow @375.
- **S13c (v1.0.6) — auto-update was NEVER working in any shipped build; found and fixed.** Root cause (proved by
  attaching an inspector to the INSTALLED app's main process): `require('electron-updater')` throws **Cannot find
  module** — electron-updater lived in devDependencies since day one (commit 7d1ba64) and electron-builder packs only
  production `dependencies` into the asar, so every installer v1.0.0→v1.0.5 shipped WITHOUT the updater; the try/catch
  in main.js made it a perfectly silent no-op (no check, no error, nothing). Earlier doc claims that the chain was
  "live/proven" were wrong and are corrected. FIX: electron-updater moved to `dependencies` (v1.0.6); verified by
  running the freshly built win-unpacked app under --inspect: the module loads and a real packaged checkForUpdates
  round-trips. CONSEQUENCE for users: installs of v1.0.5 and older need ONE manual reinstall (README warns them);
  from v1.0.6 on, updates are genuinely automatic (launch + 4h re-check + the manual button from S13b).
- **S13b (v1.0.5) — visible, on-demand updates.** The desktop updater only checked ONCE at launch, silently — an
  always-open HUD never re-checked, and a failed/raced check was invisible with no retry. Now: a **"↻ Check for
  updates" header button** (desktop only) with visible states (checking… / downloading % / update ready / you're on
  the latest vX / couldn't reach GitHub), a **4-hour periodic re-check** while running, `checking`/`none` update-status
  relays, and the installed **app version shown in the footer** (distinct from the game-save version in the header).
  Background checks stay quiet — feedback only when the user asked. (Superseded within the hour by v1.0.6, which fixes
  the deeper bug above that made all of this moot in shipped builds.)
  **F1 History + per-stage gold/hr (goals #2/#3, save-only):** the HUD now records its OWN lean snapshot per save change
  (IndexedDB `tbh-hud-history`, separate from the `tbh-hud` handle store; loaded on startup, merged with the game's
  rolling backups, capped 2400, cleared on Disconnect like the loot timeline). **Per-stage farming rates** from the
  calibrated combat-gold counter (Type 2/Sub 1) attributed to `currentStageKey` over CLEAN single-stage intervals only —
  offline gold excluded by construction (it lands in Sub 2/3). Verified vs test/live.es3 + 11 backups: **Act 2-8 ·
  Sacred Tomb ≈ 84,911 gold/hr vs Act 1-6 ≈ 36,313** — the old "best farming stage isn't derivable" deferral is now a
  MEASURED answer (Trends ranking + Lifetime + Overview one-liner; honest caveats: clean intervals, includes idle,
  sharpens over time). verify_save.js gained invariant assertions for all new fns (still PASS).
  **F2 Build Advisor (new tab):** gear-gap finder (per equipped item, an UNEQUIPPED owned item of the SAME GEARTYPE that
  is strictly better — higher rarity or same-rarity-higher-level; greedy 1:1, provable upgrades only — hand-verified vs
  the whole gear dump: exactly 1 true gap in the test save, Slayer Iron Axe→War Axe); rune plan (cheapest-first within
  gold, real per-level cost table, save-for target); open enchant slots on the deployed party (fill state only, no RNG
  claims); Party breakdown gained a **Total row** (base+gear+tree summed per stat; runes/pet still listed separately).
  **F3 Crew leaderboard (goal #14, OPT-IN):** new Crew tab — shared crew-code + display name, "Share my progress"
  OFF by default, pushes ONLY calibrated brag-stats (name, max stage, lifetime gold, kills, gold, top-3 hero levels,
  runes, Legendary+ count, play hours — never the save), board polls ~30s, rank-by selector, latest achievement derived
  server-side from each member's own snapshot deltas (new max stage / new Legendary+ / hero level-up / rune milestone),
  gap-to-you, copy-invite-code; sharing disabled in demo mode so sample data can't reach a real crew. **Backend:**
  `api/progress.js` + `api/leaderboard.js` (Vercel serverless, @neondatabase/serverless) + Neon Postgres (`tbh_crew_*`
  tables, auto-bootstrapped; ~20-snapshot history/member), deployed as **tbh-crew-api** (fusiondatacompany-projects)
  with DATABASE_URL in Vercel env (never committed); CORS-allowlist Pages+Vercel origins, `*` for the desktop (file://).
  Live-verified end-to-end: join → "Joined the crew", improved push → "Reached Act 2-10", board returns the member; the
  dashboard Crew tab verified against the live API with the real save. **Inline↔Node engine parity verified in-browser**
  (same gearGaps/per-stage numbers from the same save). Fixed a crew-chip overflow @375 (now 0 overflow, all 11 tabs).
